# Pairs with HandOffBound. Another range delete's close closes every marker of the
# tree, not only its own intent's, recording the heads it read. The intent still
# holding L keeps admitting, and its next write, stamped with the shared
# re-claimed generation, is allocated above those heads while L's marker reads
# closed.
MODULE: HandOffBoundOtherIntentClosesMarker
TARGET: HandOffBound
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: another range delete's close closes the marker of the intent still holding L
PERTURBS: OtherIntentClose

--- FIND
    /\ fFence' = fEpoch + 1
    /\ UNCHANGED <<next, author, hoOpen, hoClosedAt, windows, fAdmit, fpend, fkind, fstamp, restarted>>
--- REPLACE
    /\ fFence' = fEpoch + 1
\* MUTATION: it closes L's marker too.
    /\ hoOpen' = FALSE
    /\ \E h \in CloseHeads : hoClosedAt' = Max2(hoClosedAt, h)
    /\ UNCHANGED <<next, author, windows, fAdmit, fpend, fkind, fstamp, restarted>>
--- END
